Grove PATCH-33: ZANO must verify the scratch wallet it just installed

Asked on 2026-09-11: make sure the security work upstream has done for XMR is
inherited by the two follower coins. It is not inherited the same way by both,
because they are not related the same way:

    class ZEPHInterface(XMRInterface)   -> inherits. 60 methods, 7 overridden,
                                           none of them a guard.
    class ZanoInterface(CoinInterface)  -> a SIBLING. ~57 same-named methods,
                                           every one written independently.

So ZEPH got upstream 10ee0843 ("xmr: guard against wrong-wallet reads made
possible due to the preceding optimization commit") for free, and ZANO got
nothing. An audit of the seven XMR safety mechanisms found ZANO carrying six of
them -- the existing-spend recovery branch, the unlock-time check, the
unlocked_balance check, the wallet mutex, the transient-error classification and
the main-wallet identity confirmation are all present and all documented -- and
missing exactly this one.

WHAT XMR GUARDS, AND WHY ZANO NEEDS THE SAME PROMISE

Upstream's optimization (740360dc) stopped issuing open_wallet on every
operation. That made it possible for a stale latch to leave the WRONG wallet
open, so 10ee0843 added a postcondition at both points where the coin-B lock is
read and spent:

    open_wallet_addr = self.rpc_wallet("get_address")["address"]
    if open_wallet_addr != address_b58:
        raise TemporaryError("... refusing to spend coin B lock")

ZANO reaches the same place by a different road. It never relies on "whichever
wallet is open": every call names self.rpc_wallet_scratch explicitly, and
findTxB/spendBLockTx re-provision that connection to the joint address with
generate_from_keys immediately before use. That is a genuinely stronger design
and it is why the stale-latch bug cannot occur here.

But it has no postcondition. createWallet checks that SOME address came back and
returns; nothing compares it to the address that was asked for. If
generate_from_keys ever installs something other than the requested wallet -- a
version skew, a partially-applied patch, a key/address disagreement in the
caller -- the balance read in findTxB and the spend in spendBLockTx both run
against the previous swap's joint wallet, and neither notices. The amount check
is not a backstop: two swaps of the same size read identically.

WHY HERE RATHER THAN AT THE CALL SITES

XMR checks at read time because that is the only place it can: its wallet is
selected by a latch it does not control. Zano is handed the answer directly --
generate_from_keys returns the address it installed -- so the check belongs at
provisioning time, where it is one comparison instead of an extra RPC per call,
and where it covers every future caller of createWallet rather than the two that
exist today.

TemporaryError, not ValueError, deliberately: it matches what XMR raises, and it
keeps a transient wallet hiccup from marking a live bid BID_ERROR. A correct
swap can never trip it -- the caller derives address_b58 from the same keys it
passes -- so the only behaviour change on a healthy path is none.

Scope: ZANO only. ZEPH needs nothing; it inherits both XMR call-site guards
unmodified, which scripts/swap/verify-xmr-security-inheritance.py now asserts by
parsing the class hierarchy rather than grepping for a token.

Upstream candidate: no. ZanoInterface is Grove's own module (PATCH-15).

diff --git a/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py b/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py
--- a/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py
+++ b/basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py
@@ -482,6 +482,18 @@
         rv = self.rpc_wallet_scratch("generate_from_keys", params)
         if "address" in rv:
             new_address: str = rv["address"]
+            # PWNDA-PATCH-33: the wallet it installed must be the wallet we asked
+            # for. generate_from_keys hands the address straight back, so this
+            # costs one comparison and closes the ZANO half of upstream 10ee0843
+            # ("guard against wrong-wallet reads"), which ZEPH inherits from
+            # XMRInterface and ZANO -- a sibling of CoinInterface, not a subclass
+            # of XMRInterface -- inherits nothing of.
+            requested: str = params.get("address", "")
+            if requested and new_address != requested:
+                raise TemporaryError(
+                    "ZANO generate_from_keys installed {}, not the requested {}; "
+                    "refusing to use this wallet".format(new_address, requested)
+                )
             is_watch_only: bool = "spendkey" not in params or params.get("spendkey", "") == ""
